SPDX-FileNotice: retrods local patches, not part of upstream vice-libretro.

1. 0001-disable-resid.patch
   include/config.h turns on both reSID and FASTSID, and VICE's resolver picks
   reSID for the default SidEngine. reSID's 6581 filter tables alone are 21 MiB
   of .bss (opamp_rev[1<<16], gain[16][1<<16] and the summer/mixer offset
   tables), which does not fit a DS or a DSi.

2. 0002-sid-engine-fallback.patch
   With reSID compiled out, an explicit request for it (the SID-engine option
   still defaults to it) made set_sid_engine() return -1, so VICE silently kept
   its dummy engine. Fall back to FASTSID instead.

Applied with: patch -p1 < patches/vice-libretro/000N-*.patch
